description.narrative:
The main objective of UN Women's Strategic Note (Country Programme) 2025-2028 is to contribute to Colombia's efforts to address the challenges and opportunities regarding gender inequalities and to strengthen the empowerment of women and girls starting from their participation in peacebuilding, human security, social justice, and social protection, as well as their role as defenders of the environment and their contribution to the acceleration of the Sustainable Development Goals in a context that guarantees their right to a life free of violence.

UN Women will concentrate its work in four of the five pillars prioritized by the UNSCDF signed with the government of Colombia in June 2024:

1) Consolidation of total peace, human security and social justice.

2) Social protection and socioeconomic inclusion, with emphasis on populations in situations of vulnerability, migrants and refugees;

3) Environment, climate action and energy transition; 

4) Enablers of the 2030 Agenda.
